{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru","id":947117,"title":"Storypath System Preview now available on DriveThru","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T11:26:17-07:00","id":947117,"title":"Storypath System Preview now available on DriveThru","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/187949.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview\" target=\"_blank\"> Storypath System Preview - Onyx Path Publishing | Trinity Continuum | Scion 2nd Edition | Dystopia Rising: Evolution | They Came From Beneath the Sea! | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Storypath System Preview - The evolution of the Storypath system is tied to our work on the&nbsp;Trinity Continuum, a world of hope, heroism, and peril </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With our first look at some of the new sigs on the cover, and some Scion examples of modes of play inside.<br /> <br /> Can you share who's on the cover, Neall? I recognise Eric, Aaron, and the new Tuatha Scion, and that <i>looks</i> kinda like Annie X, one of 1e's Deva Scions, on the back...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 08-09-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:38:45-07:00","id":947126,"title":"","content":"I'm liking all the parts so far, but I'll admit some of it is kind of confusing because stuff like attributes and the intrigue system aren't laid out here. Are they unchanged from the earlier previews we saw? Or, failing that, not so different that we can't look at that to help understand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:57:33-07:00","id":947138,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the preview has me totally hyped for Scion, but I'm not sure what I can actually <i>do</i> with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:12:00-07:00","id":947149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru#post947117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...System-Preview</a><br /> Can you share who's on the cover, Neall? I recognise Eric, Aaron, and the new Tuatha Scion, and that <i>looks</i> kinda like Annie X, one of 1e's Deva Scions, on the back...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scion of Kali? at the back looks really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:55:13-07:00","id":947175,"title":"","content":"I'm already looking forward to making the Intrigue rules core in all of my chronicles and never touching the Action-Adventure ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:00:16-07:00","id":947180,"title":"","content":"I had a major hangup with Stunts on my first readthrough, but now that I get it after reading it a few times, I really like how they're executed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:04:29-07:00","id":947213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947138#post947138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the preview has me totally hyped for Scion, but I'm not sure what I can actually <i>do</i> with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a preview, not an Early Access. Our core system isn't going to change too much, but it's meant to show ease of play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you share who's on the cover, Neall? I recognise Eric, Aaron, and the new Tuatha Scion, and that looks kinda like Annie X, one of 1e's Deva Scions, on the back... </div> </div> </div>Eric Donner, Scion of Thor; Aaron Tigrillo, Scion of Tezcatlipoca; Eileen Bran, Scion of the Dagda (the Red Man of All Knowledge); Annie X, Scion of Kali. The lady with the whip is Omolara Muhammed, Scion of Oya Iyansan; the kid with the Members Only jacket and white cap is Colwyn &quot;Little&quot; M\u00e1o, Scion of Laozi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:18:32-07:00","id":947474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947213#post947213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a preview, not an Early Access. Our core system isn't going to change too much, but it's meant to show ease of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the kickstarter provide any kind of early access for other components of the base system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:19:17-07:00","id":947517,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited to see similarities between Aspects in FATE and this Path mechanic in Storypath. The new edition of Unknown Armies has a similar setup where if you can say &quot;because I'm a _____, I can...&quot; and it seems really elegant. I'm really curious to see some example Paths. Do we know how many a character gets?<br /> <br /> While Hero is definitely the good stuff here, I imagine Origins will work just fine as a standalone game, and that sounds awesome to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-10-2016, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:42:14-07:00","id":947653,"title":"","content":"Man, I'm fascinated by the idea of myth in modernity.<br /> <br /> How did Zeus feel when people stopped accepting &quot;because I'm a god&quot; as an excuse for terrible behavior?<br /> <br /> What do the Aesir think about the fact that most people (I presume) would not consider the eternal battles of Valhalla something worth fighting for, even if they qualified for it?<br /> <br /> Does a standard Western burial or cremation even <i>count</i> as proper funeral rights for the Netjer (Is that the right name for the Egyptian gods)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:05:07-07:00","id":947739,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of the Books of Magic comic book series, when protagonist Tim Hunter runs across Cupid who has reinvented himself as the Gangsta of Love, wherein Cupid eventually loses it and asks Tim if he realises how hard it's all been on him in modern times, where he's best known as a fat diaper-clad kid with a bow and arrow on stupid greeting cards on Valentine's Day.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wow. Longest running sentence either. I feel great shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:20:55-07:00","id":947748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947653#post947653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I'm fascinated by the idea of myth in modernity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The extreme tension between this and &quot;modern myth&quot;, which is the eternal power and recurrence of stories that are important to an antecedent culture, are fascinating to me. If only I could work them into a game.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait. I totally can!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:20:20-07:00","id":947790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947517#post947517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very excited to see similarities between Aspects in FATE and this Path mechanic in Storypath. The new edition of Unknown Armies has a similar setup where if you can say &quot;because I'm a _____, I can...&quot; and it seems really elegant. I'm really curious to see some example Paths. Do we know how many a character gets?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Hero-level character gets three - Origin (related to Genesis), Role, and Pantheon (your relationship with parent and pantheon). Callings are chosen to match these three Paths, and at least one of them <b><i>must</i></b> be the same as your divine parent's.<br /> <br /> (You also get to channel one Purview of your parent for free, no strings attached, no relic needed, but you only get to pick one)<br /> <br /> One of the playtest characters in the Alpha was Sigr\u00fan Askrd\u00f6ttir. Carved from a living ash by Loki\u2019s own hand, Sigr\u00fan spat her first breath back in his face, cursing Loki for giving her a masculine shape and fleeing from his sight. Taking her other parent\u2019s name\u2014the ash tree she once was\u2014she ventured across Vanaheim, walking amongst the spirits of the land, the streams, the hills, and the lakes\u2014these were, after all, her kin. After learning the magic of the trees and spurning her father once more, Sigr\u00fan eventually came to Midgard, descending the World Ash until one of its roots became an ash grove in Bethesda, Maryland.<br /> <br /> Sigrun's Origin Path, related to her Created Genesis, is <i>Loki-Carved.</i><br /> Her Role Path, related to how she learned her primary set of skills and profession, is <i>She to Whom the Woods Whisper </i>(though &quot;<i>Daughter of Vanaheim&quot; </i>would work just as well).<br /> Her Pantheon Path, related to how she once again defied and spurned her father, is <i>Loki-Defying</i>.<br /> <br /> She chooses two Skills apiece for her Origin and Role Paths, which can stack (her Pantheon Path Skills are already chosen for her - I believe the Aesir get Close Combat and Occult). These are considered Asset Skills, which means they can benefit from Path evocations.<br /> <br /> Loki's Callings are <i>Creator, Trickster, and Liminal</i>. While <i>&quot;</i>She to Whom the Woods Whisper&quot;pretty much screams Sage, &quot;Loki-Carved&quot; could be Creator or Liminal, while Loki-Defying could be either Trickster or Judge, so Sigrun herself has plenty of Callings to choose from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:33:37-07:00","id":947798,"title":"","content":"I am really excited. I love that this time scaling is built into the game rather then added on. Damage taking on more Fate characteristics is always a good thing, as well as characters being able to identify as a god's scion while still doing their own thing. The amount of effort and time put into researching myth and then translating it into a game. I can't lie, I am really looking forward to this game, probably more then I have for anything else in a very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:20:16-07:00","id":947849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947798#post947798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really excited. I love that this time scaling is built into the game rather then added on. Damage taking on more Fate characteristics is always a good thing, as well as characters being able to identify as a god's scion while still doing their own thing. The amount of effort and time put into researching myth and then translating it into a game. I can't lie, I am really looking forward to this game, probably more then I have for anything else in a very long time.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Super</i> stoked. I'm excited about a lot of things I'm hearing from the Storypath system games, it seems every single feature is something noteworthy.<br /> <br /> Take the &quot;Cinematic Pacing&quot; angle the Preview mentioned. I think I'm going to like where they go with this, deliberately patterning play through the lens of &quot;episodes, arcs, and seasons&quot; sells imagining the game as a blockbuster movie/tv/web series. They seem to be seriously close to hitting my mechanical rigidity - narrative structure sweet spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:09:35-07:00","id":948046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947849#post947849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the &quot;Cinematic Pacing&quot; angle the Preview mentioned. I think I'm going to like where they go with this, deliberately patterning play through the lens of &quot;episodes, arcs, and seasons&quot; sells imagining the game as a blockbuster movie/tv/web series. They seem to be seriously close to hitting my mechanical rigidity - narrative structure sweet spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Man, our campaign totally jumped the shark after the eighth session.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T03:43:19-07:00","id":951025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=947790#post947790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Example of Character paths*</div> </div> </div> </div>This may or may not count as minor thread necromancy, but I want to see how easy it is to create or define a character using these guidelines.<br /> <br /> Let's use the game's first iconic character and my personal favorite, Eric Donner as of his Hero stage for this example.<br /> <br /> Eric is the son of Thor, so his Origin path is pretty clear - <i>Son of Thor</i>.<br /> <br /> He was raised in the Midwestern United States by his mechanic grandfather, and was a high school football star, so let's go with <i>Blue Collar Athlete</i> as his Role path.<br /> <br /> As to his relation to his pantheon, Eric seems to have accepted his parentage (Thor's absentee parenting will probably come up later) by following in his father's footsteps as a gallant protector of the weak, so let's go with <i>Defender of Man</i>.<br /> <br /> Thor's Callings haven't been revealed yet, but it's a sure bet that <i>Guardian</i> and <i>Warrior</i> are two out of three. Origin and Role could both provide the <i>Warrior</i> Calling, while &quot;Defender of Man&quot; is basically a shoe-in for Guardian. &quot;Blue Collar Athlete&quot; might also logically give access to the <i>Creator</i> Calling and the Forge purview, representing Eric's mechanical capabilities inherited from his grandfather.<br /> <br /> Hm. Does this sound right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T06:15:27-07:00","id":951066,"title":"","content":"Yes, that sounds right. Because Paths come with two Asset Skills apiece, and Callings have three Skills apiece, congrats! You're more than halfway through character creation.<br /> <br /> Eric gets to channel one Purview from his father for free; since Giantsbane covers Sky, taking Forge makes a lot of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-15-2016, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:59:28-07:00","id":951330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=951066#post951066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that sounds right. Because Paths come with two Asset Skills apiece, and Callings have three Skills apiece, congrats! You're more than halfway through character creation.<br /> <br /> Eric gets to channel one Purview from his father for free; since Giantsbane covers Sky, taking Forge makes a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I think this Path thing might really help me out in making characters, since usually I have a problem with figuring out an interesting backstory for them. Three points of definition rather than the usual one for a character concept might really get the creative energies going!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 08-15-2016, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:32:58-07:00","id":951344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/947117-storypath-system-preview-now-available-on-drivethru?p=951330#post951330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool. I think this Path thing might really help me out in making characters, since usually I have a problem with figuring out an interesting backstory for them. Three points of definition rather than the usual one for a character concept might really get the creative energies going!</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a crunchier version of FATE Aspects, and borrowing mechanics from FATE is only a good thing in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}